--TEST--
`$a = &$b;` is `E0701` in every position it can be written, never a panic — `rule:types/implicit-capture`, `rule:classes/two-copy-depths`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// Novis has no references at all: `rule:types/implicit-capture` removed by-reference capture, so
// no binding aliases another, and `rule:classes/two-copy-depths` makes the right-hand side a copy.
// So `= &` has no owner in either rule — a refusal, not a missing lowering.
int $b = 1;
int $a = 2;
$a = &$b;

// An element target takes the same answer, and takes it once: the `&` is
// refused before the write target is even considered.
array<int> $rows = ["0" => 1];
$rows["0"] = &$b;

// PHP's other spelling of the same thing, inside an expression rather than as
// a statement of its own.
int $c = ($a = &$b);
echo "unreached\n";
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0701]: a binding cannot be assigned by reference
  --> %s:7:1
  |
7 | $a = &$b;
  | ^^^^^^^^ this would share `$b`'s own slot
  = help: Novis has no references, so remove the `&`. The assignment then copies the value. To change a caller's variable, use an `inout` parameter. To share one value that changes, put it in an object and assign the object

error[E0701]: a binding cannot be assigned by reference
   --> %s:12:1
   |
12 | $rows["0"] = &$b;
   | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this would share `$b`'s own slot
   = help: Novis has no references, so remove the `&`. The assignment then copies the value. To change a caller's variable, use an `inout` parameter. To share one value that changes, put it in an object and assign the object

error[E0701]: a binding cannot be assigned by reference
   --> %s:16:11
   |
16 | int $c = ($a = &$b);
   |           ^^^^^^^^ this would share `$b`'s own slot
   = help: Novis has no references, so remove the `&`. The assignment then copies the value. To change a caller's variable, use an `inout` parameter. To share one value that changes, put it in an object and assign the object

